CORE
test_isempty_nondet
--max-nondet-string-length 100 --function test_isempty_nondet.checkIsEmpty
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
--
Verifies String.isEmpty() == (String.length() == 0) for a nondet string.
This forces the call into the string-refinement loop because the simplifier
cannot fold isEmpty on a non-constant string, exercising
string_constraint_generatort::add_axioms_for_is_empty under the cbmc-CORE
profile.
